# microchip_sam.resc -- Renode platform + firmware load for the SAME70-style
# Cortex-M7 vendor platform in the holoscan_mcu_lite multi-vendor harness.
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   A 2 MiB flash mapped at 0x00400000, 384 KiB of SRAM at 0x20400000, one
#   console UART and the LoadELF of this board's demo image. Deliberately NO
#   network MAC, NO FMC (external SDRAM) and NO cache: this smoke test sends and
#   receives nothing, and an FMC window here would be an invitation to claim
#   memory the image is not built against.
#
# MEMORY MAP (kept in sync by renode/scripts/selfcheck_vendors.sh against
# firmware/platform/gcc_microchip_sam_hml_mcu.ld, firmware/platform/
# board_config.h and the microchip_sam row of renode/boards/index -- all four
# must agree or the microchip_sam_renode_selfcheck CTest test fails)
#   0x00400000  2 MiB   FLASH   code, rodata, .data initialiser image
#   0x20400000  384 KiB SRAM    .data, .bss, stack, newlib heap
#   0x400E0800          UART0    the only peripheral (THR +0x00, LSR +0x05)
#
# NEITHER ADDRESS IS A CANONICAL ARM ONE. Flash is not 0x08000000 and SRAM is
# not 0x20000000. Both are written out in full here because this file is where
# a plausible-looking copy-paste from a more familiar STM32-style map would
# silently produce an image the emulated machine has no memory for.
#
# ABOUT THE CORTEX-M7
#   cpuType is "cortex-m7" with nothing else enabled. No cache, no MPU, no FPU
#   and no double-precision FP: the image is compiled -mfloat-abi=soft, enables
#   no cache and configures no MPU. The platform model is thereby allowed to
#   HAVE those features without the image touching them, which is the intended
#   state. Turning a cache on inside this .resc would make the image behave
#   DIFFERENTLY from every compile of it, so nobody should.
#
# ABOUT THE UART MODEL NAME
#   No SAME70 UART model that this harness has ever seen exists to it and Renode
#   is not installed anywhere this matrix was written, so this row asks for
#   UART.NS16550 -- the same stand-in decision as the nxp_lpc row -- and
#   firmware/platform/startup_microchip_sam.c writes that block THR/LSR to match.
#   The two halves agree, which is what lets the image print at all; the base
#   address is the SAME70's UART0, and the register block is emphatically NOT the
#   SAME70 USART register map. Both halves must change together before real
#   silicon is involved. The SAME70 UART0 interrupt line (recorded as 35) is a
#   guess from the Harmony+ table; no data sheet was available to check it, and
#   no run would notice a wrong value because the demo takes no interrupt.
#
# WHY THE HEAP IS IN SRAM AND SMALLER THAN THE BASE PLATFORM'S
#   hml_reasm_open(&r, 0) uses the library default frame size of 1 MiB and
#   mallocs TWO buffers, i.e. 2 MiB of heap, which is why the BASE platform
#   (renode/holoscan_mcu_lite.resc) needs its 4 MiB SDRAM window. This board is
#   built with --frame-bytes 131072: 266 KiB of heap inside 384 KiB of SRAM,
#   after an 8 KiB stack. Same code paths, same checks, smaller frame cap.
#
# STATUS -- READ BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE
#   This platform description HAS NEVER BEEN EXECUTED. The machine this matrix
#   was written on has no Renode, no mono, no dotnet, no arm-none-eabi-gcc, and
#   github.com and downloads.renode.io are unreachable from it. Nothing here has
#   been loaded by a Renode release, and no SAME70 data sheet was available to
#   check the interrupt line against.
#   That is exactly why the CTest test that uses it exits 77 (skipped) when the
#   tooling is missing. If the tooling IS present and the platform does not load,
#   run_vendor_smoke.sh returns the emulator's non-zero exit and the test FAILS --
#   loudly, and never as a pass that was not observed.

:name: microchip_sam
:description: microchip_sam vendor platform (SAME70-style Cortex-M7, flash @ 0x00400000, UART0 @ 0x400E0800, 2 MiB flash, 384 KiB SRAM, no SDRAM, no cache). Emulator only; never executed; not silicon.

$elf?=microchip_sam_hml_mcu_demo.elf

mach create "hml_microchip_sam"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString
"""
cpu: CPU.CortexM @ sysbus
    cpuType: "cortex-m7"
    nvic: nvic

nvic: IRQControllers.NVIC @ sysbus 0xE000E000
    -> cpu@0

flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x00400000
    size: 0x200000

sram: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x20400000
    size: 0x60000

uart: UART.NS16550 @ sysbus 0x400E0800
    -> nvic@35
"""

sysbus LoadELF $elf
# The Cortex-M takes its initial SP and reset vector from the first two words of
# the region LoadELF placed the image in. On this part that is the start of the
# 0x00400000 flash window, so the offset is written out literally even though it
#   works out to zero: the point of writing it out is that selfcheck_vendors.sh
#   can
# assert the VectorTableOffset equals the linker script's FLASH ORIGIN.
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x00400000

# No showAnalyzer: under renode-test --console the UART is captured by the robot
# file's Create Terminal Tester, and an interactive analyzer window would only
# add a way for the run to fail for a non-code reason.